{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03127",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.09,
      "end_seconds": 5.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Hello? Doctor? I was told to come in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.44,
      "end_seconds": 10.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.87,
      "end_seconds": 16.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. I'll stay and fill in anything that's missed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.7,
      "end_seconds": 25.67,
      "duration_seconds": 7.97,
      "text": "It's bloating when I slip up. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.87,
      "end_seconds": 28.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.42,
      "end_seconds": 33.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Around about a month, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 35.04,
      "end_seconds": 39.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "I think it's been nearer about two months, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.43,
      "end_seconds": 46.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly one to two months. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.78,
      "end_seconds": 51.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Yes, um, somewhere around that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.6,
      "end_seconds": 60.36,
      "duration_seconds": 8.76,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.95,
      "end_seconds": 75.97,
      "duration_seconds": 15.02,
      "text": "A five out of ten, I suppose. Yes, gluten. That makes it worse. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.66,
      "end_seconds": 81.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "What about a rash on your elbows, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.27,
      "end_seconds": 98.35,
      "duration_seconds": 15.08,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, two months. As for tiredness, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.72,
      "end_seconds": 102.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.72,
      "end_seconds": 117.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.07,
      "end_seconds": 144.55,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 74, respiratory rate 16, temperature 36.6. And pressure 119 over 78."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.38,
      "end_seconds": 161.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "And what about weight loss, bone pain, vomiting or diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.3,
      "end_seconds": 167.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "No, no weight loss, bone pain, vomiting or diarrhoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.21,
      "end_seconds": 171.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.53,
      "end_seconds": 174.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.55,
      "end_seconds": 181.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.04,
      "end_seconds": 186.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "No, not that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.45,
      "end_seconds": 189.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.97,
      "end_seconds": 195.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.34,
      "end_seconds": 200.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Alright, what line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.02,
      "end_seconds": 207.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.47,
      "end_seconds": 226.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 227.56,
      "end_seconds": 238.83,
      "duration_seconds": 11.27,
      "text": "He is on lansoprazole, 30 milligrams, before breakfast, I give it to him. He takes iron tablets, once a day for my blood count."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.71,
      "end_seconds": 247.89,
      "duration_seconds": 7.18,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.77,
      "end_seconds": 251.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "I have acid reflux."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.46,
      "end_seconds": 255.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Is there anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.06,
      "end_seconds": 260.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "I have low haemoglobin, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.34,
      "end_seconds": 272.94,
      "duration_seconds": 11.6,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. Putting together what you've described, it fits best with coeliac disease on a gluten-free diet with some accidental exposure. Iron deficiency is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.31,
      "end_seconds": 277.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.78,
      "end_seconds": 299.49,
      "duration_seconds": 21.71,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now coeliac disease on a gluten-free diet with some accidental exposure is my leading thought, not anything worse. I'd like to arrange a blood count for coeliac follow-up. I'll request coeliac antibodies, it'll help with coeliac follow-up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.49,
      "end_seconds": 303.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Do I need to prepare?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.72,
      "end_seconds": 312.87,
      "duration_seconds": 8.15,
      "text": "Check labels carefully and use separate toasters and chopping boards. I'll also refer you to the dietitian."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 318.39,
      "end_seconds": 320.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Alright, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.06,
      "end_seconds": 329.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.18,
      "text": "If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 331.1,
      "end_seconds": 332.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.72,
      "end_seconds": 343.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "Come back in twelve months. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.8,
      "end_seconds": 350.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}